## 8. ACI/EP Registration & Witchborn Certification

To ensure a secure, trusted, and interoperable mesh, all contributors building new ACI nodes, major Entity Programs (EPs), or significant forks/derivatives **MUST** become Witchborn Certified.

**The Certification Process:**

1.  **Submit a Pull Request** to https://github.com/dimentox/aci to register your creation.

2.  In your PR, add your ACI/EP descriptor to the official registry file (e.g., official_registry.json). Include:

    - Project/Node name

    - Maintainer/contact information

    - A brief description, including any unique amendments or extensions

    - A stable endpoint URL if your node is intended to serve as a public mesh endpoint.

3.  **Request "Witchborn Certification"** in the title or body of your Pull Request.

**Your submission will be reviewed for:**

- **Attribution Compliance:** Strict adherence to the license and credit requirements.

- **Law Conformity:** Proper synchronization with the canonical CLD and correct implementation of amendments.

- **Quantum Protocol Handling:** Correct implementation of warnings and safeguards if quantum features are explored.

- **Security & Sanity:** A general review to ensure your node is not a threat to the mesh.

**Upon Approval:**

- Your node/EP will be merged into the canonical **Witchborn ACI Registry**.

- Your endpoint becomes eligible for discovery by other certified nodes and for participation in official mesh services.

- You may use the official **"Witchborn Certified"** badge in your repository and documentation.

**WARNING:** No unregistered endpoint will be officially discoverable, trusted, or authorized for federation within the canonical mesh. This is a critical security measure to protect the integrity of the collective.

